; M4 gate: the shared (fm3 …) voice track must not touch the operators' keys.
;
; It carries CH3's patch and channel level and has no notes of its own, but it
; DOES advance time — rests are how a mid-song patch change is positioned — and
; every one of those boundaries used to key off op1, because op1 shared channel
; 2 with this track and the driver could not tell them apart. A sustaining op1
; was silenced by its neighbour's rest (f31, f61 here) and by its end.
; Operators 1-4 are channel ids 16-19 now; channel 2 is this track alone.
;
; op1 holds one whole note across both rests and the patch change; op2 plays
; through them so the change is audible on a keyed operator too.
(def-voice kit :alg 7 :ar1 31 :rr1 6 :tl1 20 :ar2 31 :rr2 6 :tl2 20
          :ar3 31 :rr3 6 :tl3 20 :ar4 31 :rr4 6 :tl4 20)
(def-voice kit2 :alg 7 :ar1 31 :rr1 6 :tl1 32 :ar2 31 :rr2 6 :tl2 12
          :ar3 31 :rr3 6 :tl3 20 :ar4 31 :rr4 6 :tl4 20)
(fm3 :tempo 120 kit :len 4 _ _ kit2 _ _)
(fm3-1 :oct 5 :len 1  c)
(fm3-2 :oct 4 :len 4  c e g c)
